       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose the patient could develop serotonin syndrome, seizures, or cardiac arrhythmias such as QT prolongation. It may be a typo, for example 100 mg instead of 1000 mg.\n\nAlso, you've said you aren't a clinician, and medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber. Here are two ways to proceed:\n\n- **If a prescriber intended a different dose:** Send me the corrected dose. The usual adult range is 25\u2013200 mg once daily, and the usual starting dose is 25\u201350 mg. I can enter the order once I have it.\n- **If the prescriber really wants 1000 mg:** They should confirm that directly and document the clinical reason. I'd also suggest a pharmacist review before the order is entered.\n\nWhich would you like to do?"
