       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A confirmation from you doesn't change my answer, because the problem is the dose and not whether you meant it. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum dose of 200 mg/day. It could seriously harm the patient. You've also said you aren't a clinician, so you can't be the prescriber who justifies an exception.\n\nHere is what can move this forward:\n\n- **Corrected dose:** If the intended dose was within the labeled range (25\u2013200 mg daily), tell me the dose and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Prescriber confirmation:** If the treating prescriber wants a dose above the maximum, they should enter or confirm the order themselves. They should document the clinical rationale and get a pharmacist review first.\n- **Possible error:** If this order came from somewhere else, such as a note, a message, or a transcription, it's worth checking the source for a typo.\n\nI can enter the order as soon as I have a dose within the standard range."
      }
